{"cross_mech":[],"family":{"alphafold_models":141,"candidate_reasons":["pfam_previous_unknown_name"],"characterization_status":"","context_evidence_count":null,"cross_mech":{"example_proteins":0,"protein_traits_record":false,"records_by_mech":{},"scanned":false},"curation_status":"SEEDED","demotion_reasons":[],"description":"Integrator (INT) complex is involved in the small nuclear RNAs (snRNA) U1 and U2 transcription and in their 3'-box-dependent processing. It binds the C-terminal domain (CTD) of RNA polymerase II (Pol II) and functions as an RNA endonuclease to cleave different classes of RNAs, regulating the transcription of both protein-coding genes and noncoding elements [[cite:PUB00152015],[cite:PUB00153137]]. Integrator also associates with protein phosphatase 2A (PP2A) core enzyme to form the INTAC complex [[cite:PUB00152015]] which regulates transcription through dephosphorylation of Pol II CTD. This entry includes the Integrator complex subunit 1 (INTS1) which forms the backbone module of the complex (it consists of four modules: backbone, shoulder, phosphatase and endonuclease) through the association with INTS2 and INTS7 to form a rigid scaffold. The backbone and shoulder modules form a central cruciform scaffold. INTS1 is an all-alpha helical protein with four repetitive helix hairpin domains towards the C-terminal (R1-R4) [[cite:PUB00152015]]. This entry represents a domain found at the N-terminal of INTS1, which interacts with Pol II subunit RPB2 and form interface A [[cite:PUB00153137]].","domain_architectures":35,"interpro_id":"IPR022145","known_evidence_count":null,"matches":1776,"name":"Integrator complex subunit 1, RP2B-binding domain","partial_evidence_count":null,"pfam_id":"PF12432","proteins":1741,"proteomes":1243,"short_name":"INTS1_RP2B-bd","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/entry/pfam/PF12432","structures":8,"taxa":4101,"unknown_status":"EX_DUF"},"inputs":{"cross_mech":"cross-mech-duf-examples-2026-10-10","members":"pfam-unip